The attached image illustrates the physical characteristics of Nano-11 nanoparticles. The left panel, a Transmission Electron Microscopy (TEM) image with a 50 nm scale bar, reveals spherical particles with irregular, "cauliflower-like" surfaces, which are mostly singular but occasionally appear in pairs. The right panel displays a dynamic light scattering histogram, showing that Nano-11 particles have a relatively uniform hydrodynamic diameter, predominantly ranging from 30 to 110 nm and centered around 75-80 nm, consistent with the dendrimer-like alpha-D-glucan structure described in the PDF.